ESP-IDF v5.5.5, components/esp_hid: the NimBLE HID host never handles a BLE
keyboard's HID service. Two misplaced braces in the characteristic loop:

 - the report-map and report code sat inside the Device Information branch,
   after two 'continue's, so it could never run;
 - within it, the report characteristics were the 'else' of "is the report map
   readable?", so they fell to 'continue' too (and an unreadable report map
   would have written through an unset 'report' pointer).

The keyboard connects and bonds, but its report map is never read and its input
reports are never subscribed, so it sends nothing. Applied to a copy of the
component by esp-vim/CMakeLists.txt.

